page-agent (https://github.com/alibaba/page-agent)
  crates/page-runtime/js follows page-agent's page-controller, itself derived in part from
  browser-use's DOM tree script: in page_tree.js the cursors that mark a control, popup toggles
  and mouse-handler attributes as clickable, scrollable areas found by their scrollbar style and
  reported with how far they still scroll, controls listed inside a link or card when they act
  on their own, the field facts on a line (input kind, placeholder hint, date format, popup kind,
  new tab, component state) and the page position; in page_actions.js scrolling an app shell's
  main area when the document can't scroll, and the script click's innermost target, focus and
  pointer leaving the last target. Under the MIT license:

